1
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:09,000
So much food.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,840
I brought all this food back.

3
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:11,800
Couldn't help it.

4
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:12,720
I just eat a lot.

5
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:13,760
That's a lot.

6
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:16,600
They're handing breakfast out

7
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:17,480
downstairs.

8
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,640
I was wondering why everyone's
in the kitchen.

9
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:21,920
Yeah, they're handing out
food downstairs.

10
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:27,960
♪A heart once unfamiliar♪

11
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:32,320
♪Is suddenly coming alive♪

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,040
♪With you here♪

13
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:42,200
You look pretty good from this angle.

14
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:44,720
You look good from every angle.

15
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:46,560
He always knows what to say.

16
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:47,960
Then from now on,

17
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:48,960
I'll talk to you like this.

18
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:49,760
From this angle.

19
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:51,360
But my right side looks better.

20
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:52,960
Is there really a difference?

21
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:54,240
They look the same.

22
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:55,280
Just equally average.

23
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:56,560
Nothing really stands out.

24
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:03,160
Meng's all by herself.

25
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:11,320
(Looks around)
She doesn't know what to do by herself.

26
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:17,040
She went out.

27
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:22,620
(Gets water)

28
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,920
Zero gravity, then recline the seat.

29
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:26,240
Zero gravity, right?

30
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:27,160
Did we take an extra one?

31
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:28,360
There's only one.

32
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:29,040
You two can split it.

33
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:30,320
Thanks.

34
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:30,880
Sorry.

35
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:32,640
I'm hungry again.

36
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:35,240
Go ahead. I'll make you something.

37
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,240
That's too much trouble.

38
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:39,240
I'll put my share with yours.

39
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:40,000
Then you can...

40
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:40,560
Okay.

41
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:41,440
Put it in my bag.

42
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,120
Just put it with yours.

43
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:44,960
Meng looks so lonely.

44
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:56,500
(Meng leaves the small lounge)

45
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:57,840
Meng left.

46
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:00,800
Maybe she wants some time alone

47
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:02,000
to clear her head.

48
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:15,140
(The Book of Answers)

49
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:16,560
Heart's Answer.

50
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:17,840
My "mixing guide".

51
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:19,560
Let me see your "mixing guide".

52
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:21,760
"Mixing guide".

53
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:23,200
My mixing guide.

54
00:02:26,460 --> 00:02:30,180
(Sun Qimeng)

55
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:38,740
(Loneliness can push us
to connect with others)

56
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:40,480
Loneliness can push us

57
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:41,600
to connect with others.

58
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:43,560
That's so accurate.

59
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:04,800
Meng

60
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:05,640
left again.

61
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:06,360
From a professional standpoint,

62
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:07,560
they can return it without even moving.

63
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:07,960
No.

64
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:08,800
Normally,

65
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,520
you'd be running around
if you couldn't reach it.

66
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,080
That's mine.

67
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:16,160
Who's that?

68
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:16,880
Hi.

69
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:17,600
Meng.

70
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:19,280
Hey, guys.

71
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:24,760
I'm gonna sit

72
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:25,720
on the swing for a bit.

73
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:26,880
She doesn't want to bother them.

74
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:28,520
Wanna play badminton?

75
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,560
The three of us can play together.

76
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:30,880
(Invites)
We'll play in a bit.

77
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:31,480
Okay.

78
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:38,420
(Sobs)

79
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:39,760
She's hurting.

80
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:44,720
She always quietly

81
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:45,800
cries by herself.

82
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:46,480
Yeah.

83
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:48,280
Meng's afraid
of putting pressure on others.

84
00:03:58,780 --> 00:03:59,700
(Tears up)

85
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:00,480
She's crying.

86
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:04,320
She couldn't hold it in anymore.

87
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:07,180
(Cupid, Dai Xu)
It's okay.

88
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:08,640
It's okay.

89
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:19,240
Do you

90
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:21,360
just bounce it back like that

91
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:23,360
whenever you don't
feel like picking it up?

92
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:25,200
She's crying while watching them laugh.

93
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:26,240
That makes it hurt even more.

94
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:45,200
My heart hurts for her.

95
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,080
You really feel for her

96
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:11,600
because she's only trying to heal.

97
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:13,800
She knows when she needs to be alone.

98
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:15,680
She's only trying to heal.

99
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:16,120
I feel for her.

100
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:19,360
I think everyone feels lonely sometimes.

101
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:21,030
(Loneliness is a part of life)
And in those moments,

102
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:21,480
you feel so sad.

103
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:23,080
You really want someone

104
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:23,640
to be with.

105
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:25,520
You don't even have to do anything.

106
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:27,240
Just being together recharges you.

107
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:27,840
Chaoyue,

108
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:29,160
do you ever feel lonely?

109
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:29,600
I do.

110
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:31,360
Whenever I used to get really bored,

111
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:31,760
I'd

112
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:33,280
call Xiao Qi, Lai Meiyun.

113
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:33,920
I'd say,

114
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:35,280
"I'm coming over to hang out,"

115
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:35,800
or something.

116
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,160
We'd each do our own thing,

117
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:39,000
but it was really healing.

118
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,760
(A friend's company
can be the best comfort)

119
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:43,360
Now I'm more used
to dealing with those feelings.

120
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:44,000
You just

121
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,600
quietly observe them,

122
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:47,000
and then

123
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:47,880
with time,

124
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,280
they naturally pass.

125
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:51,280
(Emotions gradually fade with time)
They move through you, then leave.

126
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:52,440
That's introspection.

127
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:52,800
Yeah.

128
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:54,040
That's introspection.

129
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:55,960
It's like having a third-person view.

130
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:56,880
You step outside yourself

131
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,000
and observe yourself.

132
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:58,720
Right.

133
00:05:58,720 --> 00:05:59,240
Sami,

134
00:05:59,240 --> 00:05:59,600
why

135
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:01,000
do we feel this way?

136
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:01,920
Actually, loneliness

137
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:03,400
is a big part

138
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:04,200
of our personal

139
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:04,880
growth.

140
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:05,760
Some people

141
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:06,360
try

142
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,920
to avoid feeling lonely

143
00:06:07,920 --> 00:06:09,240
by doing

144
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:10,480
all kinds of other things.

145
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:11,520
(Staying distracted)
So they

146
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:12,880
feel less alone.

147
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:14,240
But in turn,

148
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,360
they value

149
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:16,600
their connections

150
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:18,520
with others even more.

151
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:20,200
Connections between people

152
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:22,480
(Asking for help builds bonds)
often starts with asking for help.

153
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:25,000
(Relationships nurture personal growth)
We grow through relationships.

154
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,320
I agree with that.

155
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:27,000
Yeah.

156
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:31,280
Wanna go kayaking?

157
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:33,120
Kayaking?

158
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:35,000
Kayaking.

159
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:35,720
Kayaking?

160
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:37,440
Let's wait till it warms up.
It's too cold.

161
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:38,960
It's freezing.

162
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:40,760
I'll go see how cold it is.

163
00:06:55,820 --> 00:06:57,060
(Notices)

164
00:06:57,240 --> 00:06:58,840
Did she go kayaking?

165
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,760
Did Meng go kayaking?

166
00:07:06,820 --> 00:07:08,740
(Greets)

167
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,840
What's wrong, Meng?

168
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:14,720
Are you guys playing badminton?

169
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:18,080
Let's go together.

170
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:19,760
Let's go together.

171
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:20,560
What's going on?

172
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:21,920
Did you two plan to go kayaking?

173
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:23,480
You two made kayaking plans?

174
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:24,920
They're confused.

175
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:25,920
I don't know. I'll ask.

176
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:27,160
Yeah, ask her.

177
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:29,760
What's going on?

178
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:31,800
Are you okay?

179
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:32,800
I'm fine.

180
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:35,080
Want a tissue?

181
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:36,400
Yeah.

182
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:37,700
(Pulls out a tissue)

183
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,160
But this tissue

184
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:40,960
got a little crumpled in my pocket.

185
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,280
If you don't mind...

186
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:43,280
I haven't used it.

187
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:44,400
It's fine.

188
00:07:44,660 --> 00:07:46,040
(Laughs)

189
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:47,000
She laughed.

190
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:50,000
We can all go kayaking together.

191
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:50,680
All four of us.

192
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:50,960
Yeah.

193
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:52,520
Do you wanna kayak?

194
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:54,200
I really do.

195
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:55,680
But what's wrong with Meng?

196
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:56,840
It's okay.

197
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:58,760
It's okay. Meng looks pretty
even when she cries.

198
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,040
Every angle.

199
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:02,360
Not a single bad angle.

200
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:04,840
She's so good with words.

201
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,960
Friendship between girls

202
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:07,920
is so sweet.

203
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:11,480
I just feel like...

204
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:13,520
What's wrong, Meng?

205
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:14,680
No,

206
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:15,120
Meng said

207
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:16,720
she was worried she'd interrupt us.

208
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:18,520
But we wanna kayak too.

209
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:19,320
Us?

210
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:21,080
It's okay.

211
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:23,600
Here, wipe your tears again, Meng.

212
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:24,680
Everyone's comforting her.

213
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:25,600
What do you...

214
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:26,080
You pick.

215
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:27,800
Badminton or kayaking?

216
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:29,180
Pick one.

217
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:30,800
- We'll do it together.
- Then let's kayak.

218
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:31,480
We're already dressed for it.

219
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,560
Let's go kayaking.

220
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:34,240
(Suggests kayaking together)
They're such good friends.

221
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:35,560
You guys pick.

222
00:08:35,560 --> 00:08:36,400
You two wear blue.

223
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:37,080
We'll wear pink.

224
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:37,600
I'll wear pink.

225
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:38,200
Okay.

226
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:39,960
Can we race?

227
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:40,880
Sure.

228
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:42,240
Won't we get soaked?

229
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:43,480
A little workout.

230
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:44,720
Then let's get a workout in.

231
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:45,720
We ate too much,

232
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:46,240
right?

233
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:50,680
Is this a men's one?

234
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:52,240
Why's it so tight?

235
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,000
It's a little small.

236
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:56,680
Too many push-ups.

237
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:57,040
You know?

238
00:08:57,060 --> 00:08:57,920
(Gets it)

239
00:08:57,920 --> 00:08:58,480
Those...

240
00:08:58,480 --> 00:08:59,800
Those workouts really paid off.

241
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:01,880
He can't fasten it.

242
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:04,800
It's already at your waist.

243
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:10,880
They come in different sizes.

244
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:11,880
Yeah, there are different sizes.

245
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:13,300
(Switches life jackets)

246
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:19,720
Then we'll take pink.

247
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:20,320
You guys take blue.

248
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:20,600
Sure.

249
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:21,080
It'll match better.

250
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:21,760
Meng, is that okay?

251
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:24,080
Then we'll...

252
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:25,600
When she's with friends,

253
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:26,760
she feels much better.

254
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,960
Is this one flat?

255
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,680
Did it lose air?

256
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:33,080
Yeah, it's a little flat.

257
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:34,280
Looks like it lost air.

258
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:35,960
(Blue kayak is deflating)

259
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:36,560
You guys go first.

260
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:37,440
We'll wait.

261
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:39,560
We'll cheer you on.

262
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:40,240
Okay.

263
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:40,880
You get in first.

264
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:41,760
I'll go first.

265
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:43,080
Which side, Meng?

266
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:44,200
I'll sit over there.

267
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:45,880
Wait.

268
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:47,480
Let me loosen this rope.

269
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:48,730
(Steps right in)
Don't be so fearless.

270
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:49,360
Easy.

271
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:50,080
Wait.

272
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:50,800
Slow down.

273
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,160
Why's there water inside?

274
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:54,280
Why's this seam coming apart?

275
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:55,400
I think it's leaking.

276
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:56,280
Yeah.

277
00:09:56,280 --> 00:09:57,480
Yeah, come back first.

278
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:58,680
Don't get soaked.

279
00:09:58,680 --> 00:09:59,840
It's...

280
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:00,920
It's leaking underneath.

281
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:01,960
No, the seam came apart.

282
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,440
Yeah, I noticed it came apart too.

283
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,050
(Pink kayak is leaking)
Why is this...

284
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,160
This is pretty...

285
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:07,480
I can see a gap here.

286
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:08,400
The bottom's leaking.

287
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:09,120
Yeah.

288
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:10,160
This one's fine.

289
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:11,720
But that one's flat.

290
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:12,520
That's a little risky.

291
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:13,960
I think this seam came apart.

292
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:15,920
Yeah, this kayak might be...

293
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:17,400
(Silence)

294
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:18,640
They can't use it.

295
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:20,320
Can we pump this one up?

296
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:22,080
It hasn't lost that much air.

297
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:23,120
Just a little should do.

298
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:23,680
Yeah.

299
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:25,320
This one's leaking. Not sure what to do.

300
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:27,480
But today's weather is actually perfect

301
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:28,880
for kayaking.

302
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:30,580
(Notices)

303
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:35,320
When you're already upset,

304
00:10:35,320 --> 00:10:36,680
one more thing going wrong...

305
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:37,880
Just makes it worse.

306
00:10:40,520 --> 00:10:42,200
Should we play badminton instead?

307
00:10:42,520 --> 00:10:43,280
Or...

308
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:48,520
Okay.

309
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:56,880
I can't play.

310
00:10:58,480 --> 00:10:59,320
Meng, you know what?

311
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:00,200
Two...

312
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,680
Two people can sit here.

313
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:02,720
Come here.

314
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:03,360
Okay.

315
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:04,880
Careful.

316
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:06,360
You can do that?

317
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:07,840
Push from each side.

318
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:08,680
Yeah.

319
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:09,600
Come on.

320
00:11:09,600 --> 00:11:11,440
Ready? One, two, three, go.

321
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:12,980
(Smiles)

322
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:14,720
Nice.

323
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:16,320
Nice.

324
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:19,320
This feels so nice.

325
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:23,480
Si is so cute.

326
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:24,320
Si,

327
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:24,960
I remember you

328
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,520
said swings are your favorite.

329
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:26,840
Yeah.

330
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:28,200
I still remember that.

331
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:29,640
How's the swing?

332
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:30,840
Pretty good.

333
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:33,040
Guess we don't need a kayak.

334
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:34,160
We can just

335
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,520
swing right into the water.

336
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,640
You two wanna try?

337
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:39,880
I think we'll pass.

338
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:41,240
Wouldn't the two of us

339
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:42,400
look kinda weird?

340
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:46,440
Girls can cuddle up.

341
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,280
But two guys...

342
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:49,000
We really don't need to.

343
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:51,520
Yeah, no.

344
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,480
We'll push you two.

345
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:56,120
I don't think we'd fit anyway.

346
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:57,200
Actually, maybe we could.

347
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:59,000
The girls already asked you.

348
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,560
They're trying to cheer Meng up.

349
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:02,680
(Still resisting)
We could just...

350
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:03,320
We really won't fit.

351
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:03,960
I've tried this before.

352
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:05,080
We'll sit facing opposite ways.

353
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:10,840
Let them try.

354
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:11,640
Sure.

355
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:13,520
I'll stop it.

356
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:15,760
You guys try.

357
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:18,640
Get on.

358
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:19,640
Like this.

359
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,240
Like this?

360
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:22,920
Yeah, this is the only way we fit.

361
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:29,360
I've never seen

362
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:30,640
anyone sit on a swing like that.

363
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:32,600
Does that even make sense?

364
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:34,800
Maybe put the racket down.

365
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:36,760
(Laughs)

366
00:12:36,760 --> 00:12:38,040
No...

367
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:39,480
You two...

368
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,000
How are you sitting?

369
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:41,680
Cui Yihang, like this.

370
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:42,560
Cui Yihang, you okay?

371
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:43,520
Yeah.

372
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:44,800
This is way too funny.

373
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:45,880
You two, seriously.

374
00:12:45,880 --> 00:12:47,280
Is the tree okay?

375
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,730
(I'm fine)
Are we a little too heavy?

376
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:51,320
Together we're about 150 kg.

377
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:53,480
Three, two, one. Push them!

378
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:54,840
Even the tree's bending down.

379
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:58,480
Gotta tuck your legs in.

380
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:00,600
I tucked them in.

381
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:03,380
(Bye)

382
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:05,960
His shoes are gone.

383
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:06,960
His shoes fell off.

384
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:14,760
They're all trying to cheer Meng up.

385
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:16,680
That almost hit my leg.

386
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:17,520
I don't have shoes on.

387
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:19,000
Stop messing around.

388
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:19,640
His shoe fell off.

389
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:20,640
He really doesn't have shoes on!

390
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:22,200
He threw his shoes off!

391
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,480
Where are your shoes?

392
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:27,280
He threw them off!

393
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:30,680
Meng's laughing.

394
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:31,200
That's good.

395
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:32,240
That's what matters.

396
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:34,000
I need to move my leg.

397
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,120
There's something in my way.

398
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:38,200
That "something" is his foot.

399
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:04,320
So sweet.

400
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:05,600
She's happy now.

401
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:06,880
Looking at it now,

402
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:08,400
Meng said all the right things

403
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:09,200
on her date,

404
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:10,440
but deep down,

405
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:11,440
she still

406
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:12,800
couldn't really settle

407
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:15,280
her emotions.

408
00:14:16,080 --> 00:14:18,400
She's torn between logic and emotion.

409
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:19,040
Right.

410
00:14:19,040 --> 00:14:20,040
After all, Zhao Xilun

411
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:20,880
had a place in her heart

412
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:22,000
for a while.

413
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:23,880
You can't just kick him out overnight.

414
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:25,600
I think she's probably

415
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:27,400
considered leaving.

416
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:27,960
Yeah.

417
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,960
But she's made so many friends here.

418
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:31,280
She's happy,

419
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:32,400
(Can't bear to leave her friends)
but also a little sad.

420
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:33,680
(Afraid of being alone)
Because she'd be by herself.

421
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:34,960
Sometimes,

422
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:37,160
when you see that contrast,

423
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:38,160
it really hurts.

424
00:14:38,160 --> 00:14:39,600
(Being alone isn't what hurts)
You can't help it.

425
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:40,400
(It's being alone alone)
Sometimes,

426
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:41,360
when you're the odd one out,

427
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:42,200
it can

428
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,600
make you really anxious.

429
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:44,600
You wonder, is something wrong with me?

430
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:46,240
Zhao Xilun's

431
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:47,240
cheerful approach

432
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:47,760
was to say,

433
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:49,080
"Okay, let's go kayaking."

434
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:49,520
Just like that.

435
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:50,440
He even tried to make her

436
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:51,640
laugh by going

437
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:52,880
on the swing and stuff.

438
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:53,960
That keeps Meng

439
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:54,560
from dwelling

440
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:55,560
on things she shouldn't.

441
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:57,720
She'll get

442
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:59,000
through

443
00:14:59,000 --> 00:14:59,800
this lonely

444
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:00,920
period more easily.

445
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:01,720
Yeah.

446
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:02,760
The friendships this season

447
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:04,080
have honestly

448
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:05,760
really moved me.

449
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:08,840
In this house,

450
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:10,760
romance really isn't

451
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:11,840
the only thing you gain.

452
00:15:12,530 --> 00:15:15,480
(Signal House isn't just about romance)
Family-like bonds and friendships

453
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:17,080
are beautiful too.

454
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:17,960
Yeah.

455
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:18,760
That bond

456
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:20,080
between people of the same gender

457
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:21,240
can be such

458
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:21,960
a beautiful thing.

459
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:23,360
It's really nice.

460
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:24,160
Every year,

461
00:15:24,160 --> 00:15:25,360
in the Signal House,

462
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:26,360
they form

463
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,720
really deep friendships.

464
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:42,540
(Glances toward the guys' room)

465
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:01,000
What's she thinking?

466
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,000
I'm being a bit hypocritical here.

467
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,160
One rule for me, another for you.

468
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:05,880
But

469
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:07,720
I don't need to tell you that

470
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:09,320
because you're already doing it.

471
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:11,480
Being around you is exhausting.

472
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:12,200
It's exhausting?

473
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:12,840
Very.

474
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:14,640
I don't like listening.

475
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:16,120
I like talking,

476
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:17,160
right?

477
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:19,120
So there's nothing good

478
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:20,080
about me?

479
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:20,680
No.

480
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:22,200
Because I'm just

481
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:24,160
really narrow-minded

482
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:25,520
and petty.

483
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:26,520
What if I

484
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:28,160
don't give you an invitation card?

485
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:29,080
That's fine.

486
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:35,080
Sha Yue'er.

487
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:36,480
Sha Yue'er.

488
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,560
She's thinking about what she said.

489
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:47,120
After saying all that,

490
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:48,560
she probably went back and reflected

491
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:49,560
and started feeling guilty.

492
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:51,080
Like, I shouldn't have said that.

493
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:51,680
Guilty.

494
00:16:51,680 --> 00:16:52,320
Yeah.

495
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:53,480
She said it all out of spite.

496
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:54,240
Yeah.

497
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:08,320
This room...

498
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:12,480
(Unexpected)
She went to him first?

499
00:17:16,080 --> 00:17:16,760
It's me.

500
00:17:22,980 --> 00:17:23,540
(Laughs)

501
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:24,200
Why are you laughing?

502
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,320
How are you?

503
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:26,920
You okay?

504
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:27,560
I'm good.

505
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:31,720
I think I owe you

506
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:32,960
an apology.

507
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:36,600
It's okay.

508
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:38,800
- I'm looking for the camera.
- I got too worked up that night.

509
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:39,120
It's okay.

510
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:40,600
I was pretty worked up too.

511
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:41,800
Can you wait a second?

512
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:42,440
Okay.

513
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:49,640
She smiled.

514
00:17:51,360 --> 00:17:52,360
How about we find somewhere to talk?

515
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:53,440
Chen Hewen looks so happy.

516
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:53,920
Okay.

517
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:55,160
Where do you wanna go?

518
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:55,760
Are you cold?

519
00:17:55,760 --> 00:17:57,000
You'd be cold outside, right?

520
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:57,880
(Asks)
I would.

521
00:17:57,880 --> 00:17:59,080
Then let's talk inside.

522
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:02,400
Let's talk.

523
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:03,680
Have a seat.

524
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:04,760
I'll sit on the big banana.

525
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:05,880
Okay.

526
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:08,440
Look at that smile.

527
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:11,320
How've you been

528
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,840
these past couple days?

529
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:13,920
Emotionally and everything?

530
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:17,840
I just felt really awkward.

531
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:18,560
We needed to talk it out.

532
00:18:18,560 --> 00:18:20,040
Otherwise we'd both feel uncomfortable.

533
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:23,120
I mean...

534
00:18:23,120 --> 00:18:24,880
We've only known each other a few days,

535
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:26,760
but it feels like we're always mad.

536
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:27,560
Yeah.

537
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:30,640
I'm sorry.

538
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:31,560
I thought it over,

539
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:34,160
and I really messed up a lot that day.

540
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:35,040
He apologized.

541
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:36,440
Now they're working it out.

542
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:37,360
Me too.

543
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:39,280
You didn't do anything wrong.

544
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:40,880
I messed up pretty badly.

545
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:41,400
No.

546
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:42,040
It's just

547
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:43,560
there were a lot of things I really

548
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:44,440
didn't handle well.

549
00:18:44,440 --> 00:18:45,720
Like not being considerate
of your feelings,

550
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:46,920
getting you water,

551
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:48,360
or when you were coughing.

552
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:51,760
You remember all that?

553
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:52,880
Of course I do.

554
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:55,240
He remembers it all.

555
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:56,380
(Good guy)

556
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:57,240
But

557
00:18:57,240 --> 00:18:58,040
the things I didn't do,

558
00:18:58,040 --> 00:18:59,040
I just didn't do them.

559
00:18:59,040 --> 00:19:00,400
I'll own that.

560
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:01,320
I admit I was wrong.

561
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:02,360
It was my fault.

562
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:04,680
So I don't want this

563
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,240
to make you unhappy.

564
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:07,440
Like when you cried that day.

565
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:10,840
I actually felt...

566
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:13,840
He's working up to it.

567
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:16,400
He's a little embarrassed to say it.

568
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:18,760
I really didn't handle things well.

569
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:20,120
I felt really guilty about it.

570
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:21,880
See?

571
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:25,580
(Nods)

572
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:28,200
So I started writing an apology letter.

573
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:32,520
An apology letter?

574
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:33,900
(Shocked)
Oh my God.

575
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:35,560
You really wrote one?

576
00:19:38,660 --> 00:19:39,210
(About how I acted earlier)

577
00:19:39,210 --> 00:19:39,750
(Some of the things I did)

578
00:19:39,750 --> 00:19:40,320
(Made you feel upset)

579
00:19:40,320 --> 00:19:40,680
(I'm really sorry)

580
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:41,370
(I didn't consider your feelings)

581
00:19:41,370 --> 00:19:42,180
(Instead, I focused on everyone else's)

582
00:19:42,180 --> 00:19:42,500
(I was wrong)

583
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:43,000
(I've reflected on that)

584
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:43,660
(I never meant to make you unhappy)

585
00:19:43,680 --> 00:19:44,960
So it really was an apology letter.

586
00:19:45,310 --> 00:19:46,270
Oh my God.

587
00:19:46,270 --> 00:19:47,300
(I want to make everyone happy)

588
00:19:47,300 --> 00:19:47,920
(Especially you)

589
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:48,380
(I've thought about so much)

590
00:19:48,380 --> 00:19:49,700
(All kinds of emotions were hitting me)

591
00:19:49,700 --> 00:19:50,890
(Maybe I'm not
as easygoing as I thought)

592
00:19:50,890 --> 00:19:52,740
(From my perspective,
I thought you needed space)

593
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:53,850
(I thought too much attention)

594
00:19:53,850 --> 00:19:54,610
(Would make you uncomfortable)

595
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:55,450
(I didn't ask you or talk to you)

596
00:19:55,450 --> 00:19:56,780
(I tried to guess
what you were thinking)

597
00:19:56,780 --> 00:19:58,210
(That wasn't right either)

598
00:19:58,210 --> 00:19:59,300
(I'm sorry, Sha Yue'er)

599
00:20:01,120 --> 00:20:02,040
That's kinda cute!

600
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:03,200
He even wrote an apology letter.

601
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:06,600
Yeah, I reflected too.

602
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:07,360
I thought about my behavior.

603
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:08,240
I realized

604
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:08,880
that day,

605
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:10,120
you did point out something about me.

606
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:10,720
And I agree.

607
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:11,440
You said

608
00:20:12,360 --> 00:20:13,200
I was really harsh,

609
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:13,880
right?

610
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:14,200
And...

611
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:15,040
You really were harsh.

612
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:16,000
Yeah.

613
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:16,400
I admit it.

614
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:18,320
I admit that day I probably...

615
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:19,840
did

616
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:22,040
raise my voice a little.

617
00:20:22,040 --> 00:20:22,680
So I think

618
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:24,120
I probably just

619
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:25,120
didn't manage

620
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:26,240
my emotions well.

621
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:28,600
I actually brought food yesterday.

622
00:20:28,600 --> 00:20:30,600
I wanted to talk to you.

623
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:32,800
But you got back from your date

624
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:33,600
pretty late.

625
00:20:33,600 --> 00:20:34,720
Yesterday I brought

626
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:36,520
something because you said
you like tomatoes.

627
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:39,360
So I brought tomato beef.

628
00:20:39,360 --> 00:20:40,800
I thought I'd use it to apologize.

629
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:41,640
I was like...

630
00:20:44,280 --> 00:20:45,590
Then why didn't I get any?

631
00:20:46,840 --> 00:20:47,430
Yeah.

632
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:48,400
That dish...

633
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:50,880
Near the end of dinner,

634
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:52,160
Cui Yihang and Si

635
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:53,600
were still eating.

636
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:55,440
So I reheated it again.

637
00:20:56,360 --> 00:20:57,360
You guys got back really late.

638
00:20:58,360 --> 00:21:00,480
Yesterday I thought you really hated me.

639
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:01,240
Of course not.

640
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,520
Why would I hate you?

641
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:04,320
I just hadn't figured out

642
00:21:04,320 --> 00:21:05,160
how to face you.

643
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:07,240
These past couple days,

644
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:08,040
it wasn't easy to find a chance.

645
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:09,840
Because it was date day.

646
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:12,160
It really was...

647
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:13,440
He was afraid he'd bother her.

648
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,520
That's just his personality.

649
00:21:15,520 --> 00:21:16,240
If you're there,

650
00:21:16,240 --> 00:21:17,320
shouldn't I...

651
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:18,320
Give you some space?

652
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:20,040
(Chen Hewen gives them space)
Yeah, by that logic,

653
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:22,160
I should give you two some time together.

654
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:22,880
Right.

655
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:25,760
But there's one more thing.

656
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:27,040
The invitation card.

657
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:31,280
What's wrong with that?

658
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:32,400
We all had to write one.

659
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:36,240
You gave me mine last.

660
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:38,040
But he wrote yours first.

661
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:39,600
Why didn't you give me mine first?

662
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:41,800
Why don't you mention

663
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:43,000
that I wrote yours first?

664
00:21:44,920 --> 00:21:46,080
If you wrote mine first,

665
00:21:46,080 --> 00:21:47,560
why didn't you give it to me first?

666
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:52,720
And you wrote both at the same time.

667
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:55,800
You know

668
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:57,680
who my other card was for.

669
00:21:58,200 --> 00:21:59,080
I know.

670
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:00,040
And here's why.

671
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:01,640
I got two cards that day too.

672
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:02,800
And...

673
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:05,000
I'd already written mine.

674
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:06,520
One was for you. The other was...

675
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:08,000
He knows Sha Yue'er cares,

676
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:09,080
so he won't say the name.

677
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:09,560
And

678
00:22:09,560 --> 00:22:10,880
yeah, actually,

679
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:11,920
at the time,

680
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:13,080
that day,

681
00:22:13,080 --> 00:22:15,920
Meng was crying here alone.

682
00:22:16,520 --> 00:22:17,720
You guys didn't know.

683
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:20,120
I knew, and so did (Liang Xiaoyu).

684
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:22,360
I knew and...

685
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:23,560
What's wrong?

686
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:25,200
Why's that name so hard to say?

687
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:28,840
Why?

688
00:22:29,120 --> 00:22:31,480
Because it's already pretty...

689
00:22:31,480 --> 00:22:32,960
Everyone knows, right?

690
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:33,480
Right?

691
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:35,120
It's pretty obvious.

692
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:40,760
Then that night, I got

693
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:42,040
two cards.

694
00:22:42,040 --> 00:22:43,760
One was from Meng.

695
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:46,440
So I thought,

696
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:47,000
Meng

697
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:47,760
had just been crying.

698
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:49,360
I had to consider her feelings.

699
00:22:49,360 --> 00:22:50,760
I couldn't hand you the card

700
00:22:50,760 --> 00:22:51,400
right in front of her.

701
00:22:53,040 --> 00:22:54,360
That wouldn't be great, right?

702
00:22:55,640 --> 00:22:56,240
So I thought

703
00:22:56,240 --> 00:22:57,840
I'd wait until everyone dispersed

704
00:22:57,840 --> 00:22:59,960
before giving it to you.

705
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:00,640
I get it.

706
00:23:00,640 --> 00:23:01,280
So

707
00:23:01,520 --> 00:23:03,360
that's the whole story.

708
00:23:03,360 --> 00:23:04,520
I wasn't even gonna bring it up.

709
00:23:04,520 --> 00:23:05,040
Then you...

710
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:06,840
I kept digging again.

711
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:08,120
Sorry.

712
00:23:08,440 --> 00:23:09,480
It's really pretty simple.

713
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:10,440
I just...

714
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:13,160
If I can spare someone's feelings,

715
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:14,400
I try to.

716
00:23:15,440 --> 00:23:16,000
He's just

717
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:16,800
trying to make sure

718
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:17,480
everyone's okay.

719
00:23:17,840 --> 00:23:19,160
He wants to consider everyone.

720
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:20,440
(Chen Hewen considers everyone)
Yeah.

721
00:23:23,040 --> 00:23:24,280
So,

722
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:25,560
now that I've explained it,

723
00:23:25,560 --> 00:23:27,240
do you understand me a little better?

724
00:23:28,480 --> 00:23:29,600
Fine.

725
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:30,520
I get it now.

726
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:31,680
See? Without talking,

727
00:23:31,680 --> 00:23:33,600
none of this would've come out.

728
00:23:33,840 --> 00:23:35,560
That's what mouths are for.

729
00:23:35,560 --> 00:23:36,400
Right.

730
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:37,560
You're good at talking.

731
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:38,800
You always get the best lines, Sha Yue'er.

732
00:23:39,480 --> 00:23:40,720
Of course.

733
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:47,000
But

734
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:48,440
I still don't think you know

735
00:23:48,440 --> 00:23:50,160
what actually bothered me.

736
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:52,800
Every day's a test.

737
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:57,200
What bothered you?

738
00:23:57,200 --> 00:23:58,080
Nothing I just mentioned

739
00:23:58,080 --> 00:23:58,880
was it?

740
00:24:02,160 --> 00:24:03,080
He's rubbing his hands.

741
00:24:03,080 --> 00:24:04,360
None of it.

742
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:05,280
I've already told you

743
00:24:05,280 --> 00:24:07,520
everything I know.

744
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:09,120
Can't you pick one?

745
00:24:09,480 --> 00:24:10,680
At least she asked.

746
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:11,360
That's good.

747
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:12,560
Nothing I just mentioned

748
00:24:12,560 --> 00:24:13,440
was it?

749
00:24:18,640 --> 00:24:21,120
What bothered me most
wasn't any of that.

750
00:24:21,600 --> 00:24:22,840
Then tell me.

751
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:25,120
(Rubs fingers)
He looks totally lost.

752
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:26,760
Can you think about it?

753
00:24:28,080 --> 00:24:29,480
What bothered you most...

754
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:33,640
Sha Yue'er's like,

755
00:24:33,640 --> 00:24:35,160
let's see if you can figure it out.

756
00:24:36,180 --> 00:24:38,100
(Thinks)

757
00:24:38,120 --> 00:24:40,800
Was it mentioning her around you?

758
00:24:41,680 --> 00:24:42,920
You didn't just mention her.

759
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:44,680
You wouldn't stop praising her.

760
00:24:47,760 --> 00:24:48,560
He sat up straight.

761
00:24:48,560 --> 00:24:49,820
(Sits up straight)

762
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:51,440
He stepped on every land mine.

763
00:24:52,560 --> 00:24:54,480
Even I'm getting nervous.

764
00:24:54,480 --> 00:24:54,960
When she said that,

765
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:57,040
I wanted to sit up straight too.

766
00:24:57,100 --> 00:24:57,960
(Sits up straight)
I'm scared.

767
00:24:59,580 --> 00:25:01,460
(Sits up straight)

768
00:25:01,480 --> 00:25:02,480
He just swallowed.

769
00:25:02,480 --> 00:25:04,080
He's feeling the pressure again.

770
00:25:04,080 --> 00:25:04,720
He's stressed again.

771
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:08,440
This...

772
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:08,880
honestly never

773
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:10,320
would've crossed my mind.

774
00:25:10,320 --> 00:25:10,840
I'm really sorry.

775
00:25:10,840 --> 00:25:11,640
Now that you've brought it up...

776
00:25:11,640 --> 00:25:13,080
Actually...

777
00:25:13,840 --> 00:25:15,440
At the time, it just

778
00:25:15,440 --> 00:25:17,000
never crossed my mind.

779
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:18,320
I just thought

780
00:25:18,320 --> 00:25:19,320
these were little things

781
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:20,920
that made each person special.

782
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:22,240
And when I noticed them,

783
00:25:22,240 --> 00:25:23,320
I just wanted to point them out.

784
00:25:23,320 --> 00:25:24,080
But

785
00:25:24,080 --> 00:25:25,440
from your perspective,

786
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:27,920
it probably sounded like
I was praising someone else.

787
00:25:27,920 --> 00:25:29,000
If I were you,

788
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:30,000
I'd be upset as well.

789
00:25:32,040 --> 00:25:32,840
Yeah, so I understand.

790
00:25:32,840 --> 00:25:33,680
And I...

791
00:25:33,680 --> 00:25:35,040
Yeah, I'm sorry.

792
00:25:35,040 --> 00:25:35,720
This is good.

793
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:37,280
(Nods)
This is really good. See?

794
00:25:38,120 --> 00:25:40,120
Yeah, but I really wasn't

795
00:25:40,120 --> 00:25:41,040
trying to tell you

796
00:25:41,040 --> 00:25:42,280
how great someone else was.

797
00:25:42,280 --> 00:25:43,640
I genuinely didn't mean it that way.

798
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:45,720
I just wanted to tell the whole story

799
00:25:45,720 --> 00:25:46,760
from beginning to end.

800
00:25:46,760 --> 00:25:48,360
I probably didn't think it through.

801
00:25:48,360 --> 00:25:49,480
I'm sorry about that.

802
00:25:50,040 --> 00:25:50,520
Like I said,

803
00:25:50,520 --> 00:25:52,520
I shouldn't have talked to you

804
00:25:52,520 --> 00:25:54,880
about how great someone else was.

805
00:25:54,880 --> 00:25:56,440
You never did that to me.

806
00:25:56,440 --> 00:25:57,760
That's where I fell short.

807
00:25:57,760 --> 00:25:58,240
Yeah.

808
00:25:58,240 --> 00:25:59,280
You never went on about

809
00:25:59,280 --> 00:26:00,480
how great Zhao Xilun was.

810
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:04,520
He's done for.

811
00:26:04,520 --> 00:26:06,160
He just had to bring up

812
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:07,000
how great Zhao Xilun was.

813
00:26:07,360 --> 00:26:09,200
They're arguing like a couple of kids.

814
00:26:09,200 --> 00:26:10,280
Why is he so cute?

815
00:26:11,120 --> 00:26:12,120
You never went on about

816
00:26:12,120 --> 00:26:13,360
how great Zhao Xilun was.

817
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:14,720
Yeah.

818
00:26:14,720 --> 00:26:15,640
That's something I didn't handle well.

819
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:16,720
If there's something I didn't do right,

820
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:17,680
then...

821
00:26:18,280 --> 00:26:19,520
that's on me.

822
00:26:19,520 --> 00:26:20,240
You're actually amazing.

823
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:20,920
I've always said that.

824
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:21,840
When everyone

825
00:26:21,840 --> 00:26:23,720
first got here, they all liked you.

826
00:26:23,720 --> 00:26:25,720
You obviously have
something special about you.

827
00:26:26,400 --> 00:26:27,920
I have something special...

828
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:28,520
Something very special.

829
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:30,800
But you can't say what it is.

830
00:26:30,800 --> 00:26:31,400
Of course I can.

831
00:26:31,400 --> 00:26:31,960
Why wouldn't I be able to?

832
00:26:31,960 --> 00:26:33,720
I told you the other day.

833
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:35,600
I want

834
00:26:35,600 --> 00:26:36,480
to hear it again.

835
00:26:36,700 --> 00:26:37,860
(Finds her adorable)

836
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:39,240
Say it again.

837
00:26:39,240 --> 00:26:40,320
I want to hear it again.

838
00:26:42,100 --> 00:26:43,020
(Glances at her)

839
00:26:43,320 --> 00:26:44,240
Still want to hear it.

840
00:26:47,080 --> 00:26:47,920
What stands out to me most

841
00:26:47,920 --> 00:26:49,760
is the way you look at people.

842
00:26:50,640 --> 00:26:52,160
Did you ever think of that?

843
00:26:52,840 --> 00:26:54,160
Do you know why I sometimes...

844
00:26:54,600 --> 00:26:55,480
I keep looking away,

845
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:57,520
and you think I'm not paying attention?

846
00:26:58,800 --> 00:26:59,880
I get shy.

847
00:27:00,520 --> 00:27:01,980
My face really does turn red.

848
00:27:01,980 --> 00:27:03,600
(Laughs)

849
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:04,560
It's like...

850
00:27:04,560 --> 00:27:05,800
Yeah, just like this.

851
00:27:05,800 --> 00:27:06,720
You know?

852
00:27:09,300 --> 00:27:10,740
(Too shy to keep looking)

853
00:27:10,800 --> 00:27:11,960
You can tell there's
chemistry between them.

854
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:12,600
Pure chemistry.

855
00:27:12,600 --> 00:27:13,920
Yeah, they definitely have chemistry.

856
00:27:20,460 --> 00:27:21,460
(Shy)

857
00:27:21,480 --> 00:27:22,840
And every time I look at you

858
00:27:22,840 --> 00:27:23,920
for a while,
I start thinking

859
00:27:25,040 --> 00:27:26,640
my face is about to turn red.

860
00:27:28,360 --> 00:27:29,520
And you have

861
00:27:29,520 --> 00:27:30,600
a great personality.

862
00:27:31,320 --> 00:27:32,680
Except when you're mad.

863
00:27:33,160 --> 00:27:34,400
What do you mean?

864
00:27:34,400 --> 00:27:35,600
That's a little...

865
00:27:36,040 --> 00:27:37,080
Let's not talk about that.

866
00:27:37,080 --> 00:27:38,440
Anyway, I think you have
a great personality.

867
00:27:38,440 --> 00:27:39,520
You're confident

868
00:27:39,520 --> 00:27:40,440
and easygoing,

869
00:27:40,440 --> 00:27:42,560
but still very poised.

870
00:27:42,760 --> 00:27:44,600
You still think I'm poised?

871
00:27:46,160 --> 00:27:47,240
Pretty poised.

872
00:27:47,240 --> 00:27:47,840
And you seem

873
00:27:47,840 --> 00:27:49,440
pretty happy every day.

874
00:27:50,080 --> 00:27:51,720
You seem happier than me.

875
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:54,080
There it is. The familiar vibe.

876
00:27:54,080 --> 00:27:55,800
What makes me look happy?

877
00:27:56,520 --> 00:27:57,640
I don't know.

878
00:27:57,640 --> 00:27:59,200
Here we go again
with this kind of conversation.

879
00:27:59,200 --> 00:28:00,680
I guess I'm just putting on a smile.

880
00:28:00,680 --> 00:28:01,640
Maybe.

881
00:28:01,640 --> 00:28:02,560
Really?

882
00:28:04,600 --> 00:28:05,800
"Putting on a smile" means

